---
// Figure: caching "not found" for repeated and for random missing ids.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="kv-negative" title="Caching “not found”" advance={2000}
  legend={[{ kind: 'client', label: 'Lookup for a real product' }, { kind: 'client', label: 'Lookup for an id that does not exist' }, { kind: 'hit', label: 'Answered by Redis' }, { kind: 'miss', label: 'Went to the database' }, { kind: 'write', label: '“Not found” stored' }]}
  caption="Illustrative model: two lookups a second for products that exist (all cached, so they hit) and two a second for ids that do not exist. Repeated ids come from eight missing ids with Zipf-like popularity; random ids are new every time. A “not found” entry lives 30 seconds. The filter is checked in the same round trip as the GET and wrongly says “maybe” for 1% of ids; it is kept up to date as products are created, which the model does not show. Travel times are slowed for watching.">
  <Fragment slot="params">
    <Choice name="negative" label="For ids that do not exist" value="off" options={[{ value: 'off', label: 'Cache nothing' }, { value: 'on', label: 'Cache “not found” for 30 s' }, { value: 'filter', label: 'Check a filter of real ids' }]} />
    <Choice name="missing" label="Missing ids are" value="repeated" options={[{ value: 'repeated', label: 'A few, repeated' }, { value: 'random', label: 'New every time' }]} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="absent" label="Lookups for missing ids" />
    <Readout name="share" label="Of those, reaching the database" kind="database" />
    <Readout name="sentinels" label="“Not found” entries in Redis" kind="redis" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Lookups for ids that do not exist are drawn as crossed-out circles (∅). Without negative caching, every one of them misses in Redis and goes to the database, because there is nothing to store. Lookups for products that exist keep hitting.</p>
    <p>Caching “not found” for 30 seconds absorbs repeated lookups: after the first miss for each of the eight ids, later lookups hit the stored “not found” entry, and over five minutes only about one in six lookups for missing ids reaches the database, mostly the rarely requested ones whose entries have expired. When every missing id is new, negative caching changes nothing for the database: each id misses once and is never asked for again. It only fills Redis with about 60 entries nobody will read.</p>
    <p>Checking a filter of the ids that exist stops both kinds. The filter answers “definitely not” for almost every missing id, so about one in a hundred lookups for random ids reach the database, and no “not found” entries pile up.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { mountSim, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { createScene, spread } from '../shared/scene.mjs';
  import { negative, liveSentinels } from './negative-model.mjs';
  import { dotShape } from '../shared/shapes.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="kv-negative"]').forEach(root => {
    // Lookups for missing ids are drawn as a crossed-out circle in the client grey, a shape
    // the vocabulary does not use elsewhere (a plain ring means a miss). The legend's second
    // entry shows the same shape.
    const circle = (r: number) => `M${-r} 0a${r} ${r} 0 1 0 ${2 * r} 0a${r} ${r} 0 1 0 ${-2 * r} 0z`;
    const crossed = (r: number) => `${circle(r - 0.5)}M${-r * 0.65} ${r * 0.65}L${r * 0.65} ${-r * 0.65}`;
    const legendMark = root.querySelectorAll('.cache-legend li')[1]?.querySelector('svg');
    if (legendMark) legendMark.outerHTML = `<svg class="cache-mark" data-paint="ring" viewBox="-7 -7 14 14" width="11" height="11" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="${crossed(5)}"/></svg>`;
    const fillPaint = dotShape('client').paint, ringPaint = dotShape('miss').paint;
    const scene = createScene(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Shoppers send lookups to an application, which reads Redis and, on a miss, the database.',
      nodes: [
        { id: 'clients', kind: 'client', label: 'Shoppers', count: 3 },
        { id: 'app', kind: 'app', label: 'Application' },
        { id: 'redis', kind: 'redis', label: 'Redis' },
        { id: 'database', kind: 'database', label: 'Database' },
      ],
      edges: [
        { id: 'client-app', from: 'clients', to: 'app' },
        { id: 'app-redis', from: 'app', to: 'redis' },
        { id: 'app-database', from: 'app', to: 'database' },
      ],
      layout: (width, compact) => {
        // On a narrow screen the shoppers sit higher than the application, so the first edge is longer.
        if (compact) {
          const [left, middle, right] = spread(width, 3, 30);
          return { height: 280, positions: { clients: [left, 56], app: [middle, 150], redis: [right, 62], database: [right, 220] } };
        }
        const [left, middle, right] = spread(width, 3, 90);
        return { height: 240, positions: { clients: [left, 120], app: [middle, 120], redis: [right, 56], database: [right, 182] } };
      },
    });
    mountSim(root, {
      seed: 3,
      create: (params: any, seed: number) => negative({ negative: params.negative, missing: params.missing }, seed),
      update: (model: any, params: any) => {
        if (params.missing !== model.params.missing) return false;
        model.params.negative = params.negative;
        return true;
      },
      render(model: any) {
        const active = model.movers.active();
        scene.dots(active);
        const drawn = scene.layers.dots.children;
        const r = scene.compact ? 4.5 : 5;
        active.forEach((dot: any, i: number) => {
          const el = drawn[i];
          if (!el || dot.kind !== 'client') return;
          // The scene reuses its dot elements, so set the path and paint explicitly each frame.
          const absent = !!dot.data?.absent;
          const d = absent ? crossed(r) : dotShape('client', r).d;
          if (el.getAttribute('d') !== d) el.setAttribute('d', d);
          const paint = absent ? ringPaint : fillPaint;
          if (el.getAttribute('data-paint') !== paint) el.setAttribute('data-paint', paint);
        });
        const now = model.sim.now;
        const db = model.windows.absentDb.rate(now);
        const n = liveSentinels(model);
        scene.node('database').set({ meter: db / 2, meterKind: 'database', sublabel: `${db.toFixed(1)} reads/s` });
        scene.node('redis').set({ badge: n ? `${n} “not found”` : '' });
        const t = model.totals;
        setReadouts(root, {
          absent: t.absentLookups.toLocaleString('en-GB'),
          share: t.absentLookups > 4 ? `${Math.round(Math.min(1, t.absentDb / t.absentLookups) * 100)}%` : '–',
          sentinels: String(n),
        });
      },
    });
  });
</script>
